# Shell scripts get scp'd from this Windows checkout to Linux boxes; a CRLF
# checkout silently breaks them inside tmux (tasks/lessons.md). Force LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same trap, same cure, for Quantum ESPRESSO inputs: pw.x reads Fortran namelists,
# and a trailing \r inside one is a parse error on the Linux box.
*.in text eol=lf
# ...and the restart/attempt/snapshot variants, which get scp'd and run the same way
*.in.* text eol=lf
# Queue manifests (m_*.txt) are read line-by-line by queue_r1.sh on the box; a
# trailing  lands in the nk column and breaks the launch. Force LF.
m_*.txt text eol=lf
**/m_*.txt text eol=lf

# Slurm batch scripts are scp'd to Anvil and executed by bash there: same CRLF
# trap as *.sh. So is the conda explicit lock, whose URLs a trailing \r corrupts.
*.slurm text eol=lf
qe75-explicit.txt text eol=lf

# EVIDENCE ARTIFACTS. These are pw.x / hp.x / projwfc.x outputs and their .dat
# products. They are produced on Linux, pulled to this Windows checkout, and their
# md5 sums ARE the record: runs/m_*.txt and the docs/ readouts quote them, and those
# hashes get checked against Anvil.
#
# core.autocrlf is true globally here, and every one of these files sat at
# "eol: unspecified". That means a FRESH CLONE would check them out as CRLF and every
# recorded md5 would stop matching Anvil -- the record would read as falsified on
# precisely the machine a reviewer would use.
#
# "text eol=lf", NOT "-text". -text was tried first and is WRONG here, for a reason
# worth keeping: 32 tracked .out files ALREADY sat in this worktree with CRLF (e.g.
# runs/Co_slab/H2.out, 464 CR bytes locally, 0 in the blob) because they were checked
# out under autocrlf before any attribute existed. -text means "take the worktree
# bytes as they are", so it would have COMMITTED that contamination into 32 evidence
# blobs. eol=lf normalises CRLF->LF on the way in and forces LF on the way out: it
# preserves every existing blob (verified: renormalise is byte-identical) and repairs
# the worktree on next checkout.
*.out text eol=lf
*.dat text eol=lf

# Lowdin charge artifacts. Same class of evidence as *.out, same trap, and it was
# LEFT OPEN when *.out and *.dat were fixed: `git check-attr` reported
# "text: unspecified / eol: unspecified" on all 355 tracked <job>.lowdin.txt while
# core.autocrlf is true, so a FRESH CLONE would materialise every one of them as
# CRLF. These are the A6.5(1) charge record; src/dft/extract_lowdin.py writes them
# in binary precisely so Windows cannot corrupt them, and src/dft/a0lowdin_valence.py
# revalidates them -- but neither defends against the checkout itself.
#
# Verified before adding: all 355 blobs in HEAD are already pure LF, so this rule
# is a no-op on existing content (git add --renormalize is byte-identical) and
# changes only what a clone produces.
*.lowdin.txt text eol=lf
